<item>
  <title>Day 1 of the 5-day Odissey</title>
  <dc:creator>Eva Rogelj</dc:creator>
  <link>https://vucka7.github.io/blog/posts/day_1/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 






<p>Day 1 - only beginning to dream about being a bioinformatician</p>
<p>Data Management and reproducible research <img src="https://vucka7.github.io/blog/posts/day_1/data_life_cycle.png" class="img-fluid" alt="Alt text"></p>
<p>FAIR principles</p>
<p>FAIR principles rely on good data management practices in all phases of research:</p>
<p>Research documentation Data organisation Information security Ethics and legislation</p>
<div class="quarto-figure quarto-figure-center">
<figure class="figure">
<p><img src="https://vucka7.github.io/blog/posts/day_1/fair-data-principles.webp" class="img-fluid figure-img"></p>
<figcaption>Alt text</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
<p>Best practices for file organisation</p>
<ul>
<li>There is a folder for the raw data, which does not get altered.</li>
<li>Code is kept separate from data.</li>
<li>Use a version control system (at least for code) – e.g.&nbsp;git.</li>
<li>There should be a README in every directory, describing the purpose of the directory and its contents.</li>
<li>Use file naming schemes that makes it easy to find files and understand what they are (for humans and machines) and document them.</li>
<li>Use non-proprietary formats – .csv rather than .xlsx</li>
</ul>
<p>Literate programming - Document your methods and workflows. - Document where and when you downloaded data. - Document the versions of the software that you ran.</p>
<p>Future learnings in the course: - Version control - environment managers - containers in bioinformatics - workflow manager</p>
<p>Github: Useful commands:</p>
<div class="cell">
<div class="code-copy-outer-scaffold"><div class="sourceCode cell-code" id="cb1" style="background: #f1f3f5;"><pre class="sourceCode r code-with-copy"><code class="sourceCode r"><span id="cb1-1"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># CLONE A REPO</span></span>
<span id="cb1-2">git clone https<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">:</span><span class="er" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">//</span>github.com<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">/</span>username<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">/</span>repo.git</span>
<span id="cb1-3"></span>
<span id="cb1-4"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># BASIC WORKFLOW</span></span>
<span id="cb1-5">git status                    <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># See what changed</span></span>
<span id="cb1-6">git add .                     <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Stage all changes</span></span>
<span id="cb1-7">git commit <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span>m <span class="st" style="color: #20794D;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">"message"</span>       <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Commit with message</span></span>
<span id="cb1-8">git push                      <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Push to GitHub</span></span>
<span id="cb1-9">git pull                      <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Pull latest changes</span></span>
<span id="cb1-10"></span>
<span id="cb1-11"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># BRANCHES</span></span>
<span id="cb1-12">git branch                    <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># List branches</span></span>
<span id="cb1-13">git branch new<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span>branch         <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Create new branch</span></span>
<span id="cb1-14">git checkout new<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span>branch       <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Switch to branch</span></span>
<span id="cb1-15">git checkout <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span>b new<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span>branch    <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Create and switch</span></span>
<span id="cb1-16">git push origin new<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span>branch    <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Push branch to GitHub</span></span>
<span id="cb1-17"></span>
<span id="cb1-18"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># UNDO CHANGES</span></span>
<span id="cb1-19">git restore filename          <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Undo changes to file</span></span>
<span id="cb1-20">git reset HEAD<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">~</span><span class="dv" style="color: #AD0000;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">1</span>              <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Undo last commit (keep changes)</span></span>
<span id="cb1-21">git revert HEAD               <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Undo last commit (create new commit)</span></span>
<span id="cb1-22"></span>
<span id="cb1-23"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># VIEW HISTORY</span></span>
<span id="cb1-24">git log                       <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># See commits</span></span>
<span id="cb1-25">git log <span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">--</span>oneline             <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Shorter view</span></span>
<span id="cb1-26">git diff                      <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># See what changed</span></span>
<span id="cb1-27"></span>
<span id="cb1-28"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># MERGE BRANCHES</span></span>
<span id="cb1-29">git checkout main             <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Switch to main</span></span>
<span id="cb1-30">git merge new<span class="sc" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;">-</span>branch          <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Merge branch into main</span></span>
<span id="cb1-31"></span>
<span id="cb1-32"><span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># STASH (TEMPORARY SAVE)</span></span>
<span id="cb1-33">git stash                     <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Save changes temporarily</span></span>
<span id="cb1-34">git stash pop                 <span class="co" style="color: #5E5E5E;
background-color: null;
font-style: inherit;"># Restore changes</span></span></code></pre></div></div>
</div>



 ]]></description>
